  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ajay Kumar Gupta vs The State Of Bihar on 4 October, 2016",
    "facts": "This application, for grant of anticipatory bail, arises out of Mirganj Police Station Case No. 31 of 2016, disclosing offences under Sections 272, 273, 420, 120B of the Indian Penal Code, Sections 26 (i) (iv)/31 of the Food Adulteration Act and Section 6 (A) (B) of the COTPA Act. Allegedly, a pick-up van, carrying total 16 bags, containing 6000 packets, marked with M branded chewing tobacco and 240 bags, containing 12000 packets of Madhu was recovered. The driver is said to have disclosed the name of the petitioner from whose godown the said articles were loaded.",
    "arguments": "Learned Senior Counsel, appearing on behalf of the petitioner, has submitted that his implication is based on the disclosure made by the driver of the said pick up van and there is no other material against the petitioner beyond that. He has further submitted that even if the allegations are treated to be true, no offence under Sections 272 or 273 of the Indian Penal Code is made out. According to him, strictly speaking, the petitioner cannot be prosecuted under the provisions of the Food and Adulteration Act, in view of the Division Bench decision of this Court, in the case of M/s Omkar Ajay Kumar Gupta vs The State Of Bihar on 4 October, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/161525157/ 1 Agency and Others v. The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India and Others, reported in 2016 (3) PLJR 667.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned Senior Counsel, appearing on behalf of the petitioner, has submitted that his implication is based on the disclosure made by the driver of the said pick up van and there is no other material against the petitioner beyond that. He has further submitted that even if the allegations are treated to be true, no offence under Sections 272 or 273 of the Indian Penal Code is made out. According to him, strictly speaking, the petitioner cannot be prosecuted under the provisions of the Food and Adulteration Act, in view of the Division Bench decision of this Court, in the case of M/s Omkar Ajay Kumar Gupta vs The State Of Bihar on 4 October, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/161525157/ 1",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Agency and Others v. The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India and Others, reported in 2016 (3) PLJR 667."
  },
